, {"t": 13.630416, "d": 0.315208, "w": "start"}, {"t": 13.956541, "d": 0.130416, "w": "from"}, {"t": 14.097833, "d": 0.065208, "w": "the"}, {"t": 14.173916, "d": 0.27175, "w": "same"}, {"t": 14.456541, "d": 0.315208, "w": "initial"}, {"t": 14.782625, "d": 0.434791, "w": "weights"}], "duration": 15.552708333333333, "spoken": "When the number of channels doubles from 32 to 64, our shortcut just pads the input with 32 channels of zeros. That adds no learned weights, so every residual network has exactly the same number of parameters as its plain version, and the two start from the same initial weights."}